.po 1i
.TH SETPGRP 2 Bell
.SH NAME
setpgrp \- set process group \s-1ID\s+1
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int setpgrp (\|)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Setpgrp
sets the process group
.SM ID
of the calling process to the process
.SM ID
of the calling process and returns the new process group
.SM ID\*S.
.PP
The system call
.B getpid
returns the value of the current process group.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B Setpgrp
returns the value of the new process group
.SM ID\*S.
.SH SEE ALSO
exec(2), fork(2), getpid(2), intro(2), kill(2), signal(2).
.SH ASSEMBLER
.nf
.na
	CONSTANT SETPGRP := 39

	sc	#SETPGRP
	...			!* return value in r4 *!
.fi
.ad
